No, I'm following just fine.  It's actually pretty 
simple. 

The bug, as described, makes nethack quit updating 
lighting as light sources change location.   This 
happens when the player character is blind and can't 
notice.  

In effect, this allows the character to just walk 
out of the lit radius cast by his own lit lantern - 
*while* *carrying* *the* *lantern* - if he's blind. 

This is a valid 'optimization' in vanilla nethack, 
because no standard monsters actually care about 
lighting. 

The problem is that with the 'grue' challenge, a 
monster has been introduced which actually cares 
whether the player is standing in a lit square.  A 
player carrying a lit lantern should be treated (by 
the monster) as a player standing in a lit square.  
But if the player has walked further than the radius 
of his lantern light since becoming blind, the 
monsters are treating him as standing in a dark 
square. 

